<title>FRANCE: French stocks spike up briefly after housing start.</title>
<headline>French stocks spike up briefly after housing start.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>French shares spiked up briefly after the publication of U.S. March housing starts but then retreated to levels seen before the data.</p>
<p>U.S. March industrial production due at 1315 GMT.</p>
<p>The blue-chip CAC-40 index was up 5.44 points or 0.21 percent at 2,626.07 at 1243 GMT while the CAC-40 futures contract was up two at 2,628.</p>
<p>Volume was 2.8 billion francs.</p>
</text>
